// Package testing provides the test result type used by the Binate test runner.
// Test functions return TestResult: empty string for pass, error message for fail.
package "pkg/builtins/testing"

// TestResult is the return type for test functions.  Empty means pass; non-empty
// is the failure message.  It is a *distinct* named type — not a `= @[]char`
// alias — so returning it is an explicit, type-checked label: the --test runner
// treats a `Test*` function as a test only when it returns TestResult, so a
// `Test*`-named helper that happens to return a bare `@[]char` is not picked up
// as a test.  The underlying `@[]char` is unnamed, so a plain char slice (a
// string literal, a builder result) still assigns to TestResult without a cast.
type TestResult @[]char
